Publish nothing when an odometry estimate fails.

Upstream publishes the previous pose, stamp and speed again when a scan
gives no estimate, which arrives looking like fresh odometry. Silent, the
failure reaches safety_node as stale odometry, and it brakes. A scan with
too few valid ranges counts as a failed estimate.

Upstream: https://github.com/MAPIRlab/rf2o_laser_odometry, branch ros2, at b38c68e
License:  GPL-3.0, as rf2o_laser_odometry

diff -ru a/src/CLaserOdometry2D.cpp b/src/CLaserOdometry2D.cpp
--- a/src/CLaserOdometry2D.cpp	2026-11-15 20:34:17.474328813 +0100
+++ b/src/CLaserOdometry2D.cpp	2026-11-15 20:34:17.478329486 +0100
@@ -256,19 +256,16 @@
       solveSystemNonLinear();
       //solveSystemOneLevel();    //without robust-function
     }
-    else
-    {
-      /// @todo At initialization something
-      /// isn't properly initialized so that
-      /// uninitialized values get propagated
-      /// from 'filterLevelSolution' first call
-      /// Throughout the whole execution. Thus
-      /// this 'continue' that surprisingly works.
-      continue;
-    }
 
     // 8. Filter solution
-    if (!filterLevelSolution()) return false;
+    // A scan with too few valid ranges, or one the filter rejects, has no
+    // estimate - reporting "did not move" for it would be a guess. The next
+    // scan is matched against this one, so the speed's time base moves on.
+    if (num_valid_range <= 3 || !filterLevelSolution())
+    {
+      last_odom_time = current_scan_time;
+      return false;
+    }
   } // end pyramid lvls
 
   // Get computation time 
